%   newpath mkt-q 10 20 << /Seed 9 >> mkpath mkt-flat /mkt-p2 exch def
%   newpath mkt-q 10 20 << /Seed 10 >> mkpath mkt-flat /mkt-p3 exch def
%   mkt-p1 mkt-p2 mkt-same (the same seed gives the same path) mustbe
%   mkt-p1 mkt-p3 mkt-same not (another seed gives another path) mustbe
%   rrand mkt-r0 eq (the caller's rand stream is untouched) mustbe
%   % editing the end of a formula never re-rolls its start
